        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: قضية",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قضية — qaḍiyya — \"a public issue; a cause; a court case\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تكلمنا عن قضية (qaḍiyya) الماء في القرية. takallamnā ʿan qaḍiyyat al-māʾ fī al-qarya. We talked about the issue of water in the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural قضايا, qaḍāyā. In a court it is a case."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قضية (qaḍiyya) is built on the native Arabic root q-ḍ-y, \"to decide, to settle\" (Lane). A qaḍiyya is a matter to be decided: a case, a cause, an issue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
